-- title:
--   Integral normalisation of a local conjugating element
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$, let $v$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb Q$, write $\mathbb Q_v$ for the $v$-adic completion and $\mathcal O_v$ for its valuation subring, and let $\varphi:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v\to M_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ be a ring isomorphism with $\varphi(1\otimes r)=r\cdot 1$ for every $r\in\mathbb Q_v$. For a $\mathbb Z$-submodule $\Lambda$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, let [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda\,v$ denote the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c\in\mathcal O_v$. Assume, for $\mathbb Z$-submodules $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$, that membership in the local box of $\Lambda_1$ is equivalent to all entries of $\varphi x$ lying in $\mathcal O_v$, that for some $H\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ membership in the local box of $\Lambda_2$ is equivalent to all entries of $H^{-1}\,\varphi x\,H$ lying in $\mathcal O_v$, and that $N\in\mathbb N$ satisfies $N\cdot x\in\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda_2\,v$ for every $x\in\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda_1\,v$. Then there is a unit $m$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ such that $m$ and $N\cdot m^{-1}$ both lie in $\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda_1\,v$, and such that for all $x$ one has $x\in\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda_2\,v$ if and only if $m^{-1}xm\in\mathrm{localBox}\,\Lambda_1\,v$.
--
--   This is the local end-normalisation step at a split finite place: the element conjugating one local box into the other, given abstractly by a matrix $H\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_v)$, can be replaced by a unit of the completed quaternion algebra that is itself integral and whose inverse becomes integral after multiplication by $N$. It feeds the adelic statement [`QuaternionAlgebra.exists_conjByFiniteIdele_eq_mem_finiteAdeleBox_smul_inv_mem_of_relIndex_eq`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.exists_conjByFiniteIdele_eq_mem_finiteAdeleBox_smul_inv_mem_of_relIndex_eq), where such local choices are assembled over all finite places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_exists_units_mem_localBox_nsmul_inv_mem_forall_mem_localBox_iff_of_generalLinearGroup_conj.lean

